# ⚠️ EP-034 SP-121 (T-0464) — keep HOST build artifacts out of the image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . /src` with no filter. A macOS `build/` directory in
# the working tree therefore lands in the image, and its CMakeCache.txt records
# the HOST path — so the in-container `cmake -S . -B build` aborts with:
#
#   "The current CMakeCache.txt directory /src/build/CMakeCache.txt is different
#    than the directory /Users/.../build where CMakeCache.txt was created."
#
# ⚠️ This is why the container build is fragile rather than reproducible: it
# succeeds under `--no-cache` (which regenerates the cache in place) and FAILS on
# a cached rebuild. Anyone who has run `ctest` locally poisons their next
# container build, and the error names CMake rather than the real cause.
#
# ⚠️ I-0171: `build/` alone is NOT enough — the host carries a FAMILY of build
# trees (build-tests/, build-linux-tests/, build-iphoneos/,
# build-iphonesimulator/), and any one of them entering the context reproduces
# the failure above. Match the family, not the single name that existed when
# this was written. (Filed in SP-122; hit again in SP-125.)
build/
build-*/
**/build/
**/build-*/
cmake-build-*/

# Xcode / macOS artifacts — large, and meaningless inside a Linux image.
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
.DS_Store

# VCS + editor noise.
.git/
.github/
*.swp
